  "final_message": "The root cause is in `refund_invoice` in `billing/refunds.py`. It called `successful_payments(ctx, invoice[\"customer_id\"])`, but that function takes an invoice ID. The store filters payments by `invoice_id`, so the customer ID matched no payments. The refund loop never ran, `refunded` stayed at 0, and the final check raised \"invoice has no successful payment to refund\" even though the customer had been charged.\n\n**Fix:** I changed the call to `successful_payments(ctx, invoice_id)` in `billing/refunds.py`.\n\n**Regression test:** I added `tests/test_refunds.py`. It subscribes a customer, which charges the invoice, then refunds it and checks the credit note amount. It fails without the fix and passes with it.\n\n**Tests:** `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q` reports 25 passed, up from 24.\n\n**`answer.json`:** written to the repo root with `{\"file\": \"refunds.py\", \"function\": \"refund_invoice\"}`. It is listed in `.gitignore`, so it won't show in `git status`.\n\nI did not commit anything.",
